            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Paramount's new owners to increase film production, hang on to cable networks",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "LOS ANGELES (Reuters) -Paramount Global unveiled plans on Wednesday to retain and develop its stalwart entertainment brands Nickelodeon, MTV, and BET, while sharply increasing feature film production following its $8.4 billion merger with Skydance Media.  \"We're thinking about ... the cable networks, not as declining linear assets that we need to spin off or deal with somehow,\" said President Jeff Shell.  Shell joined Chairman and CEO David Ellison and the rest of the executive team at a media gathering on Wednesday on the Paramount Pictures lot, where they discussed strategy for their film, television, and streaming businesses - as well as emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence.",
